    {
      "title": "Death toll rises to 68 with dozens injured after high-speed train collision in Spain – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/28/spain-train-crash-toledo-europe-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>Pedro Sánchez says the government will act with urgency to ‘clarify what has happened, why this tragedy occurred’</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/spain-train-crash-high-speed-toledo\">Full report from Spain</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>At least 30 people are believed to have died after two high-speed trains collided in the province of Toledo in Spain,</strong> with concerns the death toll could be much higher.</p><p><strong>The number of people affected is expected to rise </strong>(<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/28/spain-train-crash-toledo-europe-latest-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6ae1c3898f086d92d1fa1400#block-6ae1c3898f086d92d1fa1400\">10:46</a>)<strong>,</strong> local authorities said, with growing concerns about a “major tragedy” (<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/28/spain-train-crash-toledo-europe-latest-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6ae1c8358f088388a1da0008#block-6ae1c8358f088388a1da0008\">11:03</a>).</p><p>The affected trains are understood to be Iryo 7076 with 146 passengers plus one baby on board, and AVE 2080 with 397 passengers on board, making it <strong>544 people in total on board of both train </strong>(<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/28/spain-train-crash-toledo-europe-latest-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6ae1c6448f088388a1d9fffd#block-6ae1c6448f088388a1d9fffd\">11:00</a>).</p><p><strong>The incident comes less than a year after a similar crash in Adamuz,</strong> the province of Córdoba, which killed 46 and injured 152 in January this year (<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/28/spain-train-crash-toledo-europe-latest-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6ae1c6448f088388a1d9fffd#block-6ae1c6448f088388a1d9fffd\">11:00</a>).</p><p><strong>Spain’s high-speed railway network ranks as the largest in Europe </strong>and the second biggest in the world after China, carrying 25 million passengers in 2024.</p><p>Spain’s prime minister <strong>Pedro Sánchez</strong> said he was “shocked” by the accident (<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/28/spain-train-crash-toledo-europe-latest-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6ae1c49c8f086d92d1fa1405#block-6ae1c49c8f086d92d1fa1405\">11:05</a>), with transport minister <strong>Óscar Puente </strong>working at the emergency control centre to “obtain all possible information about what happened” (<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/28/spain-train-crash-toledo-europe-latest-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6ae1cb4f8f08895cb8ad8afa#block-6ae1cb4f8f08895cb8ad8afa\">11:16</a>).</p><p><em>Updated at 10:50am UK to reflect the new death toll</em></p><p><em>“In the [emergency] control center since 9:40 trying to obtain all possible information about what happened.”</em></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/28/spain-train-crash-toledo-europe-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-28T20:53:55"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘It all happened in a split-second’: survivors recount details of deadly train crash in Spain",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/it-all-happened-in-a-split-second-survivors-recount-details-of-spains-second-deadly-train-crash-in-10-months",
      "description": "<p>Passengers describe carriages full of seriously injured people after crash that has claimed at least 68 lives</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/spain-train-crash-high-speed-toledo\">At least 68 killed in Toledo train crash – full report</a></p></li></ul><p>Josimar Medina woke a little before 9am on Wednesday to find himself airborne and hurtling through his carriage on the fast train from Madrid to Seville.</p><p>“I remember flying through the air and looking for my girlfriend, who was also shooting through the air,” said Medina, a 37-year-old tourist from the northern Peruvian city of Chiclayo.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/it-all-happened-in-a-split-second-survivors-recount-details-of-spains-second-deadly-train-crash-in-10-months\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-28T18:12:01"
    },
